--- E1: the exit 0 vs return 0 bug -------------------------------
  installKicad() in install-eSim-25.04.sh ends the already-installed
  branch with 'exit 0'. Demonstration that exit terminates the whole
  script while return only leaves the function:
$ bash e1-demo.sh   (original: exit 0 inside the function)
  [kicad] already installed -> exit 0
  -> steps after the KiCad check never ran (E1 reproduced)

--- N4: the uninstall path purges an undefined variable ----------
  Original line: apt-get purge -y llvm-${llvm_version} llvm-${llvm_version}-dev
  With llvm_version unset this expands to:
    apt-get purge -y llvm- llvm--dev
  (empty package names - apt errors out, LLVM is left installed)
  Patched script defines llvm_version="18" at the top, so the same
  line purges llvm-18 llvm-18-dev clang-18.

